WEBVTT

00:01:58.375 --> 00:02:03.184
I was responsible for shaping culture
in a business of 90,000 employees

00:02:03.208 --> 00:02:05.351
in 150 countries.

00:02:05.375 --> 00:02:07.809
And I found that stories
were such a great way

00:02:07.833 --> 00:02:09.393
to connect with people

00:02:09.417 --> 00:02:11.143
and have them think,

00:02:11.167 --> 00:02:13.643
"What would I do in this situation?

00:02:13.667 --> 00:02:15.059
Would I have known Dottie

00:02:15.083 --> 00:02:18.393
or who are the Dotties
I need to know in my life?"

00:02:18.417 --> 00:02:21.434
I found that no matter people's gender
or their generation

00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.476
or their geography in the world,

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:26.351
the stories resonated and worked.

00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:27.726
But in my work with leaders,

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:31.143
I've also found they tend
to be allergic to telling stories.